        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://cityofmerrill.org/about-merrill/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Merrill is the birthplace and boyhood home of Disney comics artist Carl Barks, who created Scrooge McDuck.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merrill%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The first business established in Merrill was a grist mill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merrill%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Merrill is an agricultural area that celebrates its farming heritage with an annual Potato Festival.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merrill%2C_Oregon"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Southern Pacific and Great Northern railroads aided the economic growth of Merrill when they were completed in the early 1930s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
